# Skills exposed to a Managed Agents session that mounts this repository.
# One skill per line: a leaf directory name under skills/ (e.g. docx-official)
# or a repo-relative path (e.g. skills/game-development/2d-games).
# Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Everything a mounted repo carries in .claude/skills/ becomes agent
# instructions with no review step, in a sandbox with bash and web_fetch.
# Keep this list to what the HENRY agents actually need. The ~25
# offensive-security skills in this library are deliberately NOT here.
# `python -m engine bridge --all` bridges everything if you truly want that.

# --- operating the fleet itself ---
# (managed-agents itself is NOT bridged: a session that has mounted this repo
#  reads skills/managed-agents/ directly, and a copy would be a second source
#  of truth that drifts every time a manifest changes.)
skill-creator
verification-before-completion
systematic-debugging
test-driven-development
executing-plans
writing-plans
plan-writing

# --- quantitative reasoning (the engines CLAUDE.md tells Claude to reach for) ---
prediction-toolkit
monte-carlo-predictor

# --- strategy / finance / sales ---
brainstorming
pricing-strategy
launch-strategy
competitor-alternatives
copywriting
email-sequence
marketing-psychology

# --- documents ---
# Deliberately NOT bridged: the four *-official document skills are 73% of the
# library's bytes, and agents that need them attach Anthropic's HOSTED versions
# via `skills: [{type: anthropic, skill_id: xlsx}]`, which never touches the
# repository copy.
